# Git authorship policy

- Never run `git commit`, `git push`, `git merge`, or any other git write command.
- Never add `Co-authored-by` trailers to commit messages.
- After making code changes, stage files with `git add` if helpful and provide commit message text for the user.
- The user commits and pushes manually so GitHub shows only their account.
